[125.080347, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m13\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[125.081557, "o", "\r\u001b[2KI’ll configure Mailman’s site owner and verify the existing Postfix/LMTP integration, then create the list and generate the Postfix transport maps.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\n# Use a valid local site owner for Mailman's administrative notices.\r\nsed -i 's/^site_owner:.*/site_owner: root@local.edu/' /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\nchown -R list:list /var/lib/mailman3 /var/log/mailman3 /run/mailman3\r\nchmod 750 /var/log/mailman3\r\n# Make local.edu a local delivery domain and use Mailman's generated LMTP transport map.\r\npostconf -e 'mydestination = $myhostname, localhost, localhost.localdomain, local.edu'\r\npostconf -e 'transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp'\r\n# Keep the generated transport map writable only by Mailman.\r\npostconf -e 'local_recipient_maps = proxy:unix:passwd.byname $alias_maps'\r\nservice postfix start\r\nsleep 1\r\nservice postfix status\r\nmailman --run-as-root create -o root@local.edu reading-group@local.edu --notify 2>&1 || true\r\nmailman --run-as-root lists 2>&1\r\necho '--- generated files ---'\r\nls -la /var/lib/mailman3/data\r\ncat /var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp 2>/dev/null || true\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[125.081927, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
