[129.441532, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\npostfix/postlog: starting the Postfix mail system\r\n   ...done.\r\n * postfix is running\r\nCreated mailing list: reading-group@local.edu\r\n1 matching mailing lists found:\r\nreading-group@local.edu\r\n--- generated files ---\r\ntotal 312\r\ndrwxrwx--- 1 list list   4096 Nov  1 00:30 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 list list   4096 Nov  1 00:30 ..\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 list list 270336 Nov  1 00:30 mailman.db\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 root root    335 Nov  1 00:30 postfix_domains\r\n-rw-r----- 1 root root  12288 Nov  1 00:30 postfix_domains.db\r\n-rw-rw---- 1 root root    990 Nov  1 00:30 postfix_lmtp\r\n-rw-r----- 1 root root  12288 Nov  1 00:30 postfix_lmtp.db\r\n# AUTOMATICALLY GENERATED BY MAILMAN ON 2026-11-01 00:30:57\r\n#\r\n# This file is generated by Mailman, and is kept in sync with the binary hash\r\n# file.  YOU SHOULD NOT MANUALLY EDIT THIS FILE unless you know what you're\r\n# doing, and can keep the two files properly in sync.  If you screw it up,\r\n# you're on your own."]
